{"title":"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Seven teams play a soccer tournament in which each team plays every other team exactly once. No ties occur, each team has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7f4de02215a8c5319886c13b2e291811346e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> chance of winning each game it plays, and the outcomes of the games are independent. In each game, the winner is awarded a point and the loser gets 0 points. The total points are accumulated to decide the ranks of the teams. In the first game of the tournament, team <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> beats team <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95fbfb49b675ba11392ba7c2603d0c87f89be76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Probability\" title=\"Probability\">probability</a> that team <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> finishes with more points than team <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271cdd78c4c10cde94410584ce7282874413cb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The results of the five remaining games are independent of the first game, so by symmetry, the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> scores higher than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in these five games is equal to the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> scores higher than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. We let this probability be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />; then the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> end with the same score in these five games is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8eadf5f2d7ba4060687696673aa0aadae7c9b32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Of these three cases (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/9102c45b4c6847bf98b07d481c47e8d1d42036a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| &gt; |B|, |A| &lt; |B|, |A|=|B|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />), the last is the easiest to calculate (see solution 2 for a way to directly calculate the other cases). \n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a386f757e560bf73d9ac9826b1c2d9e783b13822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5\\choose k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"40\" height=\"55\" /> ways to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> victories, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a386f757e560bf73d9ac9826b1c2d9e783b13822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${5\\choose k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"40\" height=\"55\" /> ways for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> victories. Summing for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/3396c0524cf771796a5435ee8399fa5234e5e39a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2p = \\frac{1}{2^{5} \\times 2^{5}}\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{5} {5\\choose k}^2\\right) = \\frac{1^2+5^2+10^2+10^2+5^2+1^2}{1024} = \\frac{126}{512}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"557\" height=\"64\" /></center>\n<p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d3165d1694e4f0a0184edda5c9217ae66b0fcee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\frac 12 \\left(1-\\frac{126}{512}\\right) = \\frac{193}{512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"196\" height=\"45\" />. The desired probability is the sum of the cases when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d38c0f26be31b37d95204159a45f0fe7fd1af73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| \\ge |B|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7a9a5e2521ffcf2e592355f27991eb9c25be2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{126}{512} + \\frac{193}{512} = \\frac{319}{512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fefc741cc91ab64dadf041779ea6f9011adcf5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>You can break this into cases based on how many rounds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins out of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins 0 games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must win 0 games and the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd4b24e0e6259492c9f710addc05982ccd5e7413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{5 \\choose 0}}{2^5} \\frac{{5 \\choose 0}}{2^5} = \\frac{1}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"42\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins 1 games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must win 1 or less games and the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a3186136adbabf988e16d4af9b9c610c870dd41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{5 \\choose 1}}{2^5} \\frac{{5 \\choose 0}+{5 \\choose 1}}{2^5} = \\frac{30}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"42\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins 2 games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must win 2 or less games and the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40df27c711317b1a7b7a1316e6b81ee2e08dee20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{5 \\choose 2}}{2^5} \\frac{{5 \\choose 0}+{5 \\choose 1}+{5 \\choose 2}}{2^5} = \\frac{160}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"42\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins 3 games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must win 3 or less games and the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc3c10d39056c854c71612caa4de7f1f1829ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{5 \\choose 3}}{2^5} \\frac{{5 \\choose 0}+{5 \\choose 1}+{5 \\choose 2}+{5 \\choose 3}}{2^5} = \\frac{260}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"42\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins 4 games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must win 4 or less games and the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f02b49009ea3cbb3df79dbc35a5d67d681a2402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{5 \\choose 4}}{2^5} \\frac{{5 \\choose 0}+{5 \\choose 1}+{5 \\choose 2}+{5 \\choose 3}+{5 \\choose 4}}{2^5} = \\frac{155}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"297\" height=\"42\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins 5 games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must win 5 or less games and the probability of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a4571094b0f69dc932dd67f5b5ac42f8613ee4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{5 \\choose 5}}{2^5} \\frac{{5 \\choose 0}+{5 \\choose 1}+{5 \\choose 2}+{5 \\choose 3}+{5 \\choose 4}+{5 \\choose 5}}{2^5} = \\frac{32}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"342\" height=\"42\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Summing these 6 cases, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480f7f96dc98dd741fc76bb9a5e3809060710514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{638}{1024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36b36a967bba271d050f2df96adda23c0d3975d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{319}{512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/4493a7f0f03039dd690b97f402d5ddfee6c1ff93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319 + 512 = \\boxed{831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can apply the concept of generating functions here. \n</p><p>The generating function for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/8199e3491bbcc4037fe1a8126b80e38f40123589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + 0x^{1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" /> for the first game where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f471e446a0b38f261f3d7f9ddcf80ed434afc762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{n}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> is winning n games. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lost the first game, the coefficient for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58595d636e7df3ac0e9fd37e08532f80f34e6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{1}$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is 0. The generating function for the next 5 games is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/05500c30d6d50c8d4cc3cc0de278fab0685779ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + x)^{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, the total generating function for number of games he wins is\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4027bc3d03b15b9cd84174f3d10d9b50c5b6a19d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(1 + 0x)(1 + x)^{5}} = (1 + 5x^{1} + 10x^{2} + 10x^{3} + 5x^{4} + x^{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"429\" height=\"19\" />.\n</pre>\n<p>The generating function for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the same except that it is multiplied by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d1459f73a89d5d2bd1adcd155195fccf8f9d34bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+0x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. \nThus, the generating function for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d01dd9e7d085ee442d03cf41b1d589739f929483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1x + 5x^{2} + 10x^{3} + 10x^{4} + 5x^{5} + x^{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"273\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> wins 0 games is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99038cfb4c72100160971a30c90eaf4fd831001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Since the coefficients for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f471e446a0b38f261f3d7f9ddcf80ed434afc762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{n}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> where \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578cf6c5b8058f6f8e6369416da6dcaf73f8fc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> sums to 32, the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins more games is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77fc3e38635c6ac881ec61c42de4e78767653be8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{32}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has more wins than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/098a412f7169395e471c5781243ae876188c5383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{32} \\times \\frac{32}{32} + \\frac{5}{32} \\times \\frac{31}{32} + \\frac{10}{32} \\times \\frac{26}{32} + \\frac{10}{32} \\times \\frac{16}{32} + \\frac{5}{32} \\times \\frac{6}{32} +\\frac{1}{32} \\times \\frac{1}{32} = \\frac{638}{1024} = \\frac{319}{512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"629\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/4493a7f0f03039dd690b97f402d5ddfee6c1ff93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$319 + 512 = \\boxed{831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>After the first game, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games we care about-- those involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> wins more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> win the same number of games. Also, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf856775e3de1168a9a4f29bc68d3651d0bf6051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10} = 1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> total outcomes. By symmetry, the first and second cases are equally likely, and the third case occurs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/1998d1e371a8f544052eaeaf098e065132d0e7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{5}{0}^2+\\binom{5}{1}^2+\\binom{5}{2}^2+\\binom{5}{3}^2+\\binom{5}{4}^2+\\binom{5}{5}^2 = \\binom{10}{5} = 252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"500\" height=\"56\" /> times, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combinatorial_identity#Another_Identity\" title=\"Combinatorial identity\">a special case of Vandermonde's Identity</a>. There are therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b045fa48caf67a319146e275a43b2117b3133c8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1024-252}{2} = 386$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"140\" height=\"37\" /> possibilities for each of the other two cases.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has more wins than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> remaining games, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> cannot beat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> overall. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has more wins or if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are tied, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will beat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> overall. Therefore, out of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c2fa23f6d345eb6b967ae9416712eaecf7741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1024$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> possibilites, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8cdea910e92306c5b8cf3a81637c69ba602700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$386+252 = 638$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> ways where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins, so the desired probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46dfdd390a5480cb9ad9b2ababf6c9cdaf86a262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{638}{1024} = \\frac{319}{512}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b37b20e5b9a061ed62086fdc5614785656a3ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Like Solution 3, we use generating functions, but instead to calculate the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />'s and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />'s scores. There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability both win, giving a net result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability the difference increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> probability it decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more games for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, the game outcomes are independent, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> starts off having won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more, the generating function is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/6152b9094ca99a9c27ce7a5cb0a87f784f5d5dd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}x+\\dfrac{1}{2}+\\dfrac{1}{4}x^{-1}\\right)^5\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af2c47405de1912f597b5cbfe29fb5cd87cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{1024} \\cdot x^{-4} \\cdot (x+1)^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"167\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We wish to find the sum of all coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91e5924e876095538b15ff89f41d6ec62b7afea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,x^2,\\ldots,x^6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /> so by the Binomial Formula this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acfb161ae425a2f2be612cad07c6e262a3314d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\binom{10}{5}+\\binom{10}{6}+\\binom{10}{7}+\\binom{10}{8}+\\binom{10}{9}+\\binom{10}{10}}{1024}=\\dfrac{638}{1024}=\\dfrac{319}{512}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"419\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/6/6d61a7b8857b92c604ddab9e60c8c12956efcbd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{831}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II\" title=\"2006 AIME II\">2006 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title